      {
        "id": 184431,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-15T16:31:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now that he's unlocked, I'll say I enjoy using PW Argent just as much as I thought I would. The only real downsides are not being able to play a quickie Sarabande and Alacritous Subdominant being much less useful to play at all (since I often find that if I have one of the H-melody instruments I'm more likely to be using it on Inspiring Supertonic), but I think that's made up for by getting a free Silver Shadow and being able to stack plays even more nicely with Cadence. I also find myself being willing to use the second power of Cedistic Dissonant more often for card churn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can agree. His power makes you consider other options that you normally have to be a bit setup for, and it brings a whole new use to Arcane Cadence. It does make you more reliant on certain instruments, but that's normal for AA.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now I'm looking forward to when we get XTreme Argent and the poor Vocalize VA has to pull out a punk rocker scream.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I personally want to have that scream from the begining of Deep Purple's 'Highway Star'.</p>",
