      {
        "id": 184434,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-15T16:39:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The thing I like most about PW AA's power is how much faster he seems to set up -- by the end of turn one, chances are I've either got two songs or a song and an instrument in play <em>and</em> I was able to get something else done (either healed, helped someone else play a card, draw a bunch, or damage). Vanilla AA had a much slower build.</p><p>While I do miss being able to use the melodies right off the bat, I don't know that I'll ever play vanilla AA again.</p>",
